  "reason": "The only strong unimodal evidence so far is RNA-only with PCA and singleprofile, which substantially outperforms image-only ResNet in both accuracy and F1. The key uncertainty is whether using multiple profiles with a simple aggregation can improve on the best RNA baseline. config_002 tests this by extending the promising PCA RNA setting to multiprofile with avgpool, the simplest aggregation option, before trying more complex choices like transformer aggregation or multimodal fusion. This is an efficient next step because it exploits the strongest current direction while isolating the effect of profile aggregation with minimal added complexity."
}

